  "description": "G1, Norway Maple / Sycamore / Ash\rTo cut back all overhanging branches by 2-3m, back inline with edge of parking bays\rG2, 2 x Ash\rTo fell to a safe height (5m) and prune back trees beneath to achieve a 4m clearance from Jessop House.\rT307, Beech\rTo shorten lateral branches towards flats by up to 3m, back to a point inline with kerb at the bottom of the bank.\rT308, Beech\rTo shorten lateral branches towards flats by up to 2m, back to a point inline with kerb at the bottom of the bank.\rT311, Beech\rTo shorten lateral branches towards flats by up to 2m, back to a point inline with kerb at the bottom of the bank.\rReasons\rBeech reductions - To gain better separation from flats.\rAsh Trees - Showing significant signs of Ash dieback disease.\rG1 - Overgrown and overhanging parking bays, dropping excessive debris onto parked cars.\r(TPO 25, 1993)",
